{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PlancherelViaRecipe","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PlancherelViaRecipe","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.plancherel_via_recipe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.plancherel_via_recipe","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PlancherelViaRecipe.lean#L29-L44","doc":"**Plancherel via the recipe.**  From the Markov-trace normalization\n`∑_λ d_λ · y_λ(q) = 1` it follows that not every Wedderburn block\ncontributes zero weight: some block `λ` has `d_λ · y_λ ≠ 0`.\n\n§3b-conditional on `PlancherelViaRecipeContext`: the normalization itself is\nassumed, not established.  The conclusion is *derived* from the hypothesis\n(a sum equal to `1 ≠ 0` cannot have all terms zero) rather than projected\nfrom a conclusion field, so this is not a self-assuming projection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PlancherelViaRecipeContext.normalization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PlancherelViaRecipeContext.normalization","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PlancherelViaRecipe.lean#L27-L27","doc":"Markov-trace normalization for `H_n(q)`: `∑_λ d_λ · y_λ(q) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PlancherelViaRecipeContext.y","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PlancherelViaRecipeContext.y","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PlancherelViaRecipe.lean#L25-L25","doc":"The Plancherel weights `y_λ(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PlancherelViaRecipeContext.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PlancherelViaRecipeContext.d","kind":"def","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PlancherelViaRecipe.lean#L23-L23","doc":"The Wedderburn block dimensions `d_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PlancherelViaRecipeContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PlancherelViaRecipeContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PlancherelViaRecipe.lean#L21-L21","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PlancherelViaRecipeContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PlancherelViaRecipeContext","kind":"class","line":8,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PlancherelViaRecipe.lean#L8-L27","doc":"Context for the Markov-trace (Plancherel) normalization of `H_n(q)`.\n\n**Restated 2026-08-22** (vacuity ledger, `proof-no-trivial-true` /\n`proof-no-self-assuming-projection`).  The class previously carried the\nsingle field `holds : (1 : ℝ) = 1` — provable by `rfl`, so it constrained\nno instance, and the theorem below projected it to conclude `(1 : ℝ) = 1`:\nvacuous with *or* without an instance.\n\nThe fields now state the actual categorical input the block names — the\nWedderburn block dimensions `d_λ`, the Plancherel weights `y_λ(q)`, and the\nnormalization identity `∑_λ d_λ · y_λ = 1`.  The normalization is the lone\nconditional hypothesis (the Markov-trace normalization of `H_n(q)`, assumed\nhere, not derived). ","signatureChunk":0}]}